{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3n8ebwcW1bB67vqFDSK","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't changed or committed anything yet. A single commit conflicts with how the nightly import works, so I need you to choose an option first.\n\nThe misspelling `wholsale` appears once in each of three months: `data/2025-10.csv`, `2025-11.csv` and `2025-12.csv`. The uncommitted `data/2026-01.csv` doesn't have it.\n\n**Why one commit doesn't work:** the README says the nightly import reloads only the data file for the month the commit message starts with, so \"a commit that touches several months loads only that one.\" A single `2025-10: fix wholsale` commit would fix the repo, but the import would only reload October. November and December would keep `wholsale` downstream, and nothing would report it.\n\n**Options:**\n- **(a) Three commits, one per month (my recommendation).** Each month gets reloaded. You can still undo all three with one command: `git revert --no-edit <first>^..<last>`. I'd give you the exact range afterwards.\n- **(b) One commit as you asked.** Only the month in the message gets reloaded, and the other two would need reloading some other way. I can't see from the repo whether the import can do that.\n\nBefore committing, I'll run `scripts/check.sh` as usual. All three files are 2025, so the check does cover them this time.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":213,"cache_read_input_tokens":20519,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":213,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-51>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T00:37:2